    "preamble": "Manoj And Anr vs State And Anr (2024:Rj-Jd:9836) on 26 February, 2024 Author: Farjand Ali Bench: Farjand Ali [2024:Rj-Jd:9836] High Court Of Judicature For Rajasthan At Jodhpur S.B. Criminal Misc. Petition No. 860/2017 1. Manoj S/o Pukhraj, Caste Jain, R/o Prem Nagar Siwana District Barmer. 2. M/ s Arihant Agency Siwana Through Manoj S/o Pukhraj, Caste Jain, R/o Prem Nagar Siwana District Barmer. ----Petitioners Versus 1. State Of Rajasthan 2. Food Inspector, Office Of Chief Medical And Health Officer, Barmer, District Barmer. ----Respondents For Petitioner(s) : None present For Respondent(s) : Mr. Arun Kumar, P.P. Hon'Ble Mr. Justice Farjand Ali Order 26/02/2024 1. None present for the petitioners. 2. The impugned order has been passed way back on 13.07.2015 whereby learned Additional Chief Judicial Magistrate Balotra, District Barmer took cognizance for the offence 26[2][1] of the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006. 3. There is no interim order passed by this Court and thus, it can be presumed that much water has been flowed under the bridge.",
